            <div xml:id="d726">

                <pb facs="0864" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.1115/277: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Reval</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Albrecht</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tallinn</hi> [<hi rendition="#small-caps">Reval</hi>]</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1921-03-27T14:00:00+01:39"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March 27, 1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received
                        3:07 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>As instructed I handed Litvinoff a copy of statement in your March 25th. He
                    inquired whether this was an official reply to Moscow proposal and whether any
                    other reply might be expected. I of course told him I had no information beyond
                    what was contained in statement. Up to the present time I had avoided having any
                    intercourse with Bolshevik delegation. Does Department authorize <pb facs="0865"
                        n="769" xml:id="pg769"/> me unofficially and personally to receive Litvinoff
                    should he approach me with further proposals? This latter is but a hypothetical
                    question regarding a contingency which may or may not arise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albrecht</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
